Besiktas Club extended Necip Uysal and Utku Yuvakuran's contract for 4 years.
The Turkish Football Federation's (TFF) website found that Beşiktaş had extended the contract until 31 May 2021.
Necip, who grew up in the black-and-and-white team and completed his first professional contract on June 19, 2008, began to play for the A-team during the 2009-2010 season.
He played a total of 254 official matches for Besiktas.
The TFF website also stated that the goalkeeper Utku Yuvakuran, whom Besiktas rented in the squad last last season, received his bonservi and signed a contract until 31 May 2021.
Utku has been discontinued from temporary transfer as of August 1, 2017 and his license has been revoked on August 2.
Utku Yuvakuran served mainly in under-21 league matches in Beşiktaş, where he played last season.
The young goalkeeper only took part in a black-and-white jersey in 2 Turkish Cup matches.
